                                                                          Economic benefits is the first core objective of local tourism development. An increase in the
                                                                      number of tourists not only promotes local economic growth and increases municipal revenues,
                                                                                                      ：




                                                                      but also provides more employment opportunities for local residents, thus raising their incomes. In
                                                                      addition, economic efficiency is a key factor in sustainable tourism management strategies. When
                                                                                                     号




                                                                      the economic benefits are too low or the costs do not match the benefits, the local government may
                                                                      seek new economic growth points or even give up the continued development of tourism. Therefore,
                                                                                         信




                                                                      maximizing economic benefits should be the first objective function in the planning model.
