                                                                                                                   Memo
                                                                      To: Juneau Tourism Council
                                                                      Subject: Sustainable Tourism Management Recommendations for Juneau
                                                                            Honorable Members of the Juneau Tourism Council,




                                                                                                                                       型
                                                                          The city of Juneau is attracting the attention and love of tourists with its beautiful natural




                                                                                                                                     模
                                                                      landscape and comfortable living environment, which undoubtedly brings great economic benefits
                                                                      to the city of Juneau. However, it has been noted that due to the rapid increase in the number of
                                                                      tourists, the natural resources of the City of Juneau are being damaged and the normal life of the




                                                                                                                                   学
                                                                      residents is being disturbed by the swarm of tourists.




                                                                                                                                 数
                                                                          Our assessment of the current state of tourism development in the City of Juneau indicates
                                                                      that if no management measures are taken to limit the number of visitors or protect the natural
                                                                      environment, the number of visitors will remain above 1.6 million for the next decade, and the




                                                                                                                             ：
                                                                      most popular attraction, the Mendenhall Glacier, will disappear from its current viewpoints




                                                                                                                            el s
                                                                      within 25 years and completely recede within 90 years, which will inevitably affect the long-
                                                                                                                           号
                                                                      term tourism and economic development of the City of Juneau. As the makers of management




                                                                                                                          od
                                                                      decisions for tourism management in Juneau, it is important to develop appropriate management
                                                                                                             众
                                                                      strategies to achieve sustainable tourism. To this end, we have constructed a mathematical model


                                                                                                                       Hm
                                                                      and propose the following actionable measures to you:
                                                                                                 公

                                                                            Measure 1: Increase Visitor Dispersion
                                                                                                                    AT
                                                                         Methods: Increase publicity for niche attractions and limit visitor flow or periodically close
                                                                                                信



                                                                      popular scenic spots
                                                                                         微




                                                                          Effect: The greater the dispersion of tourists, the more balanced the number of tourists accepted
                                                                                                                   M

                                                                      by each attraction, and when the dispersion of tourists is close to 1/n (n is the total number of
                                                                                                        ：


                                                                      attractions), the greater the total benefits.
                                                                            Measure 2: Increase Tourist Consumption
                                                                                                       号




                                                                            Methods: Increase tax rates and commodity prices at scenic spots
                                                                         Effect: When the tax rate and prices increase, the number of tourists decreases and the total
                                                                                           信




                                                                      benefits increases. The total benefit is greatest when the tax rate is adjusted to 0.58.
                                                                                          微




                                                                            Measure 3: Determine the Optimal Number of Tourists
                                                                          Method: Analyze the number of tourists when the total benefits is maximum through Pareto
                                                                      optimality
                                                                          Effect: Ensure the Sustainable evelopment of regional tourism and promote the maximization
                                                                      of social benefits. The social benefit is maximized when the total number of tourists is 1.32 million
                                                                      in the year.
                                                                                                                                                                Sincerely,
                                                                                                                                                          Team #2502617
